{title: The Lord's Work}
{subtitle: Ezra 10:18–19; Nehemiah 8:4–7; 12:41–42; 11:5–7; 10:25}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bbmaj7/D] | [Eb] | [Bb] [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Among the [Bb]priests a name is found
From [Dm]the sons of Jeshua known
Maa[Eb]seiah stood with them
To [Cm7]face the weight of [F]sin
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
They [Bb]pledged to send the [Dm]wives away
[Eb]And being guil[F]ty stood in day
[Gm]A ram from flock was [Dm]offered up
To [Eb]cleanse the heart and [F]wash the [Bb]cup [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]On a wooden platform high
Ez[Dm]ra opened up the eye
Beside [Eb]him Maaseiah stood
With others [Cm7]in the crowd
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
They pledged [F]to send [Bb]the wives away
And [Dm]being guilty [Eb]stood in day
A [F]ram from flock was [Gm]offered up
To cleanse [Dm]the heart and wash [Eb]the cup
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The Le[F]vites explained [Bb]the Law [Eb][Gm7][Eb]
[Bb]While the people stood in awe
Maa[Dm]seiah spoke with clear sound
Guiding [Eb]the minds that were bound
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
They pledged to send [Cm7]the wives away
And [F]being [Bb]guilty stood in day
[Dm]A ram from flock [Eb]was offered up
[F]To cleanse the heart [Gm]and wash the cup
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Dm]Lord's work is done [Eb]with grace
In the [F]restored ho[Bb]ly place
{end_of_verse}

